cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you report a no-biology floor, a size-confound percentile, or a
  size-corrected re-ranking produced by this software, please cite both the
  software and the BioGRID ORCS data the reference distribution is built from.
title: "denali: the no-biology floor for gene-set rankings"
abstract: >-
  denali measures how much of a gene-set ranking is explained by how the sets
  were constructed - chiefly their size - rather than by biology. It ships an
  audit that reports that share with a verdict and a percentile against 1,272
  published human CRISPR screens, a size-aware re-ranking that shows which
  entries the original ranking cannot justify, a size-only baseline scored on
  the caller's own evaluation metric, and a per-screen atlas of published
  floors. The method is not novel - EGAD shipped node-degree AUROC as a
  built-in null in 2017, Crow et al. 2019 did the cross-dataset version, and
  GREAT corrects region-size bias. What is offered here is the null computed
  identically for everyone, versioned, and callable from a command line, an MCP
  server and a browser. The tool reports properties of rankings and refuses to
  nominate candidates.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Schroeder
    given-names: Alex
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandro-publius/denali"
url: "https://alejandro-publius.github.io/denali/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - gene set enrichment
  - confounding
  - reproducibility
  - null model
  - baseline
  - pathway analysis
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The BioGRID database: A comprehensive biomedical resource of curated
      protein, genetic, and chemical interactions
    authors:
      - family-names: Oughtred
        given-names: Rose
    journal: Protein Science
    year: 2021
    volume: 30
    issue: 1
    start: 187
    end: 200
    doi: 10.1002/pro.3978
    notes: >-
      BioGRID ORCS 2.0.18 is the source of the 1,272 published human CRISPR
      screens behind the reference distribution and the per-screen floor atlas.
      Cite this alongside any percentile or floor reported by denali.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Camera: a competitive gene set test accounting for inter-gene correlation
    authors:
      - family-names: Wu
        given-names: Di
      - family-names: Smyth
        given-names: Gordon K.
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    year: 2012
    volume: 40
    issue: 17
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gks461
    notes: >-
      The variance inflation factor VIF = 1 + (m-1) * rho-bar that denali's
      audit reports and that its correction is a cheaper relative of.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Predicting gene function in a hierarchical context with an ontology-aware
      network (EGAD)
    authors:
      - family-names: Ballouz
        given-names: Sara
    journal: Bioinformatics
    year: 2017
    doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btw695
    notes: >-
      Prior art, stated rather than hidden. EGAD has shipped node-degree AUROC
      as a built-in null since 2017. denali's method is not novel; its packaging
      and its atlas are what is new.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      GREAT improves functional interpretation of cis-regulatory regions
    authors:
      - family-names: McLean
        given-names: Cory Y.
    journal: Nature Biotechnology
    year: 2010
    doi: 10.1038/nbt.1630
    notes: >-
      Prior art. GREAT already corrects region-size bias in the genomic-region
      setting.
